{
  "title": "53: al-Najm النجم",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالنَّجْمِ اِذَا هَوٰىۙ‏(1)\n\nBy the star when it goeth down\nمَا ضَلَّ صَاحِبُكُمْ وَمَا غَوٰى‌ۚ‏(2)\n\nErreth not your Companion (Our Apostle Muhammad) nor is he led astray\nوَمَا يَنْطِقُ عَنِ الْهَوٰىؕ‏(3)\n\nAnd nor he speaketh of (his own) inclination\nاِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا وَحْىٌ يُّوْحٰىۙ‏(4)\n\nIt (the wording) is naught but a revelation revealed (unto him)\nعَلَّمَهٗ شَدِيْدُ الْقُوٰىۙ‏(5)\n\nTaught him the one Intense in power\nذُوْ مِرَّةٍؕ فَاسْتَوٰىۙ‏(6)\n\nThe one endued with wisdom; (and) hence he took an overviewing position\nوَهُوَ بِالْاُفُقِ الْاَعْلٰى ؕ‏(7)\n\nWhile he was in the highest horizon\nثُمَّ دَنَا فَتَدَلّٰىۙ‏(8)\n\nThen he drew nigh, and became pending\nفَكَانَ قَابَ قَوْسَيْنِ اَوْ اَدْنٰى‌ۚ‏(9)\n\nThus was (he) the measure between two bows (facing each other) or nigher still\nفَاَوْحٰۤى الٰى عَبْدِهٖ مَاۤ اَوْحٰىؕ‏(10)\n\nThen revealed He unto His Servant what He did reveal\nمَا كَذَبَ الْفُؤَادُ مَا رَاٰى‏(11)\n\nBelied not (his) heart what he saw\nاَفَتُمٰرُوْنَهٗ عَلٰى مَا يَرٰى‏(12)\n\nWhat! Dispute ye then with him as to what he saw?\nوَلَقَدْ رَاٰهُ نَزْلَةً اُخْرٰىۙ‏(13)\n\nAnd indeed he did see him at another descent\nعِنْدَ سِدْرَةِ الْمُنْتَهٰى‏(14)\n\nAt the ‘Sidra’ (the Lotetree) ‘Muntaha’ (the all-Comprehensive Terminus)\nعِنْدَهَا جَنَّةُ الْمَاْوٰىؕ‏(15)\n\nNigh unto it is the Garden-Abode\nاِذْ يَغْشَى السِّدْرَةَ مَا يَغْشٰىۙ‏(16)\n\nWhen covereth (over) the ‘Sidra’ (Tree) that which covereth it\nمَا زَاغَ الْبَصَرُ وَمَا طَغٰى‏(17)\n\nNeither his eye did dazzle nor did it rebel\nلَقَدْ رَاٰى مِنْ اٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِ الْكُبْرٰى‏(18)\n\nIndeed he did see of the greatest signs of his Lord\nاَفَرَءَيْتُمُ اللّٰتَ وَالْعُزّٰىۙ‏(19)\n\nSee ye then (the idols) Lat and the Uzza?\nوَمَنٰوةَ الثَّالِثَةَ الْاُخْرٰى‏(20)\n\nAnd Manat, the third (idol) besides?\nاَلَكُمُ الذَّكَرُ وَلَهُ الْاُنْثٰى‏(21)\n\nWhat! for you the males and for Him (God) the females?\nتِلْكَ اِذًا قِسْمَةٌ ضِيْزٰى‏(22)\n\nThis indeed is a division unjust\nاِنْ هِىَ اِلَّاۤ اَسْمَآءٌ سَمَّيْتُمُوْهَاۤ اَنْتُمْ وَاٰبَآؤُكُمْ مَّاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ بِهَا مِنْ سُلْطٰنٍ‌ؕ اِنْ يَّتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا الظَّنَّ وَمَا تَهْوَى الْاَنْفُسُ‌ۚ وَلَقَدْ جَآءَهُمْ مِّنْ رَّبِّهِمُ الْهُدٰىؕ‏(23)\n\nThey are nothing but (mere) names, which have named ye and your fathers, sent not God for them any authority; They follow nothing but a conjecture what their selves are inclined to; and indeed, hath come unto them from their Lord the right guidance\nاَمْ لِلْاِنْسَانِ مَا تَمَنّٰى   ۖ‏(24)\n\nWhat! Shall man have whatever he wisheth?\nفَلِلّٰهِ الْاٰخِرَةُ وَالْاُوْلٰى‏(25)\n\nNay! God’s is the (life) hereafter and the former (life)\nوَكَمْ مِّنْ مَّلَكٍ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ لَا تُغْنِىْ شَفَاعَتُهُمْ شَيْئًا اِلَّا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ اَنْ يَّاْذَنَ اللّٰهُ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَرْضٰى‏(26)\n\nAnd how many an angel in heavens are whose intercession is of no avail at all save after that permitteth God whomsoever willeth He and chooseth\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ لَيُسَمُّوْنَ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةَ تَسْمِيَةَ الْاُنْثٰى‏(27)\n\nVerily, those who believe not in the hereafter name the angels with female names\nوَمَا لَهُمْ بِهٖ مِنْ عِلْمٍ‌ؕ اِنْ يَّتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا الظَّنَّ‌ۚ وَاِنَّ الظَّنَّ لَا يُغْنِىْ مِنَ الْحَقِّ شَيْئًاۚ‏(28)\n\nBut they have not of it anything of knowledge; they follow nothing but a conjecture; verily a conjecture availeth naught the truth at all\nفَاَعْرِضْ عَنْ مَّنْ تَوَلّٰى ۙ عَنْ ذِكْرِنَا وَلَمْ يُرِدْ اِلَّا الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا ؕ‏(29)\n\nTherefore, turn thou aside from him who turneth his back against Our reminder, and desireth not anything but the life of this world\nذٰ لِكَ مَبْلَغُهُمْ مِّنَ الْعِلْمِ‌ ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنْ ضَلَّ عَنْ سَبِيْلِهٖ ۙ وَهُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنِ اهْتَدٰى‏(30)\n\nThat is the (last) reach of their knowledge; Verily, thy Lord knoweth best of him who is astray from His path and He knoweth best of him who is guided aright\nوَلِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِۙ لِيَجْزِىَ الَّذِيْنَ اَسَآءُوْا بِمَا عَمِلُوْا وَيَجْزِىَ الَّذِيْنَ اَحْسَنُوْا بِالْحُسْنٰى‌ ۚ‏(31)\n\nAnd God’s is whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth, that He may recompense those who do evil for what they did, and that He may recompense those who do good, with what is best\nاَلَّذِيْنَ يَجْتَنِبُوْنَ كَبٰٓئِرَ الْاِثْمِ وَالْفوَاحِشَ اِلَّا اللَّمَمَ‌ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ وَاسِعُ الْمَغْفِرَةِ‌ؕ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِكُمْ اِذْ اَنْشَاَكُمْ مِّنَ الْاَرْضِ وَاِذْ اَنْتُمْ اَجِنَّةٌ فِىْ بُطُوْنِ اُمَّهٰتِكُمْ‌ۚ فَلَا تُزَكُّوْۤا اَنْفُسَكُمْ‌ ؕ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنِ اتَّقٰى‏(32)\n\nThose who do avoid the great ones of the sin and shameful deeds save accidentally verily, thy Lord is (the Lord of) vast forgiveness: He knoweth best about you when He raised you from the earth and when ye are embryos in the wombs of your mothers; so assert ye not the purity of your selves; He knoweth best of him who guardeth (himself against evil)\nاَفَرَءَيْتَ الَّذِىْ تَوَلّٰىۙ‏(33)\n\nHast thou then seen him who hath turned his back\nوَاَعْطٰى قَلِيْلًا وَّاَكْدٰى‏(34)\n\nAnd giveth he a little and withholdeth (his hand)\nاَعِنْدَهٗ عِلْمُ الْغَيْبِ فَهُوَ يَرٰى‏(35)\n\nWhat! Is with him the know-ledge of the unseen that he seeth\nاَمْ لَمْ يُنَبَّاْ بِمَا فِىْ صُحُفِ مُوْسٰىۙ‏(36)\n\nOr hath he not been told of what is in the scriptures of Moses?\nوَاِبْرٰهِيْمَ الَّذِىْ وَفّٰىٓ  ۙ‏(37)\n\nAnd of Abraham who fully discharged (his mission)?\nاَلَّا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ وِّزْرَ اُخْرٰىۙ‏(38)\n\nThat no bearer of a burden shall bear the burden of another\nوَاَنْ لَّيْسَ لِلْاِنْسَانِ اِلَّا مَا سَعٰىۙ‏(39)\n\nAnd that there is not for man (aught) save what he striveth for\nوَاَنَّ سَعْيَهٗ سَوْفَ يُرٰى‏(40)\n\nAnd that his striving shall soon be seen\nثُمَّ يُجْزٰٮهُ الْجَزَآءَ الْاَوْفٰىۙ‏(41)\n\nThen shall he be recompensed to the fullest measure\nوَاَنَّ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ الْمُنْتَهٰىۙ‏(42)\n\nAnd that unto thy Lord is the end (of all)\nوَاَنَّهٗ هُوَ اَضْحَكَ وَاَبْكٰىۙ‏(43)\n\nAnd verily He it is Who causeth (one) to laugh and causeth (him) to weep\nوَاَنَّهٗ هُوَ اَمَاتَ وَ اَحْيَا ۙ‏(44)\n\nAnd that He it is Who causeth death and causeth life\nوَاَنَّهٗ خَلَقَ الزَّوْجَيْنِ الذَّكَرَ وَالْاُنْثٰىۙ‏(45)\n\nAnd He it is Who createth pairs, the male and the female\nمِنْ نُّطْفَةٍ اِذَا تُمْنٰى‏(46)\n\nFrom the sperm when it is discharged\nوَاَنَّ عَلَيْهِ النَّشْاَةَ الْاُخْرٰىۙ‏(47)\n\nAnd that on Him (alone) is the raising for a second time\nوَاَنَّهٗ هُوَ اَغْنٰى وَ اَقْنٰىۙ‏(48)\n\nAnd that He it is Who enricheth and bestoweth contention\nوَاَنَّهٗ هُوَ رَبُّ الشِّعْرٰىۙ‏(49)\n\nAnd that He it is Who is the Lord of Sirius\nوَاَنَّهٗۤ اَهْلَكَ عَادَا۟ اۨلْٮئُوْلٰى ۙ‏(50)\n\nAnd that He did destroy (the powerful) ‘Ad of the ancient (times)\nوَثَمُوْدَا۟ فَمَاۤ اَبْقٰىۙ‏(51)\n\nAnd Thamood, and He spared not (one to survive)\nوَقَوْمَ نُوْحٍ مِّنْ قَبْلُ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا هُمْ اَظْلَمَ وَاَطْغٰىؕ‏(52)\n\nAnd the people of Noah before; Verily they, they were the most unjust and the most transgressing\nوَالْمُؤْتَفِكَةَ اَهْوٰىۙ‏(53)\n\nAnd the cities overthrown (it is) He (Who) did overthrow\nفَغَشّٰٮهَا مَا غَشّٰى‌ۚ‏(54)\n\nSo covered them what did cover\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكَ تَتَمَارٰى‏(55)\n\nWhich then of the bounties of thy Lord wilt thou dispute about?\nهٰذَا نَذِيْرٌ مِّنَ النُّذُرِ الْاُوْلٰٓى‏(56)\n\nThis (Our Apostle Muhammad) is a Warner of the warners of old\nاَزِفَتِ الْاٰزِفَةُ‌ۚ‏(57)\n\nDraweth nigh the (Hour of Reckoning which is) ever drawing nigh\nلَيْسَ لَهَا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ كَاشِفَةٌ ؕ‏(58)\n\nNone there is for it other than God to lay it bare\nاَفَمِنْ هٰذَا الْحَدِيْثِ تَعْجَبُوْنَۙ‏(59)\n\nWhat! Wonder ye then at this statement?\nوَتَضْحَكُوْنَ وَلَا تَبْكُوْنَۙ‏(60)\n\nAnd laugh ye and not weep?\nوَاَنْتُمْ سٰمِدُوْنَ‏(61)\n\nAnd yet sport ye (negligently)\nفَاسْجُدُوْا لِلّٰهِ وَاعْبُدُوْا ۩‏(62)\n\nTherefore, prostrate ye in obeisance unto God and worship Him (alone)",
  "merits": "Surah al-Najm (The Star)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 26 verses. The reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the number of believers and sinners combined. The reciter will lead a respectable and honourable life and people will love and respect him.\nWriting this Surah and keeping it at a talisman makes one courageous in front of the ruler and makes the ruler respect him. He also comes out victorious in debates and discussions."
